# The animation bridge's props (animation design D1.1), headless: nothing is drawn, so the
# `animation` tool says what the bridge would choose for the humanoid set. The hero carries the
# sword in the right hand; the drink puts it on the hip for a while (the `drink` mount), then it
# goes back. A body without `Animated` needs the set named.

seed 42

act? ui_close screen=confirm_quit
act? ui_close screen=settings
act? ui_close screen=pause
act heal id=e5
act stop

# --- 1. at rest: the sword is in the hand; the warden carries nothing
act animation id=e5 animset=humanoid
expect result contains "e5 has no Animated"
expect result contains "carry (moveset player): sword at hand_r"
expect result contains "props: sword at hand_r"
act? animation id=e5
expect result contains "is not animated"
act content_get kind=prop id=sword
expect result contains "\"size\""

# --- 2. a drink: the sword sits at the hip through the middle of it, and is back in the hand after
# (a shared game may hold the hero mid-swing)
step 60
act use_item item=flask
step 30
act animation id=e5 animset=humanoid
expect result contains "props: sword at hip"
step 40
act animation id=e5 animset=humanoid
expect result contains "props: sword at hand_r"

# --- 3. a fix for a bad call
act? animation id=e5 animset=humanoyd
expect result contains "is not in content"
